member.summary:
One member sub-block of a : the typed common-primitive prefix plus the
member-specific parameters in source order. Members may share/duplicate keys with each other;
each member keeps its own ordered list so nothing is lost.

A group of outputs, as described by an [OutputGroupN] section (e.g. "Fabrication
Outputs", "Assembly Outputs"). A typed view over the underlying ;
 is parsed from the section's indexed OutputTypeN/OutputNameN keys.

A node in a project's logical sheet hierarchy (built from the flat
). Each node is one sheet instance: the same
document may appear at several nodes if it is instantiated by more than one sheet symbol.

True when harness records were read from the "Additional" OLE stream (kept verbatim in
). The writer then skips re-emitting them to FileHeader so they
aren't duplicated on round-trip.

Writes Altium project (.PrjPcb) files. The project file is plain UTF-8 INI-style text;
sections are emitted in  order, each followed by a single
blank line, matching Altium's layout so a read/write round-trip is byte-for-byte.
